# Sketchfab models

When adding or replacing 3D models, **use the Sketchfab Data API** — not the website, and not generic web image/model sites.

## Auth

Read `SKETCHFAB_API_TOKEN` from repo-root `.env`. Never commit `.env` or print the token.

```
Authorization: Token $SKETCHFAB_API_TOKEN
```

## Search (downloadable only)

```
GET https://api.sketchfab.com/v3/search?type=models&q=Eiffel+Tower&downloadable=true
```

A linked Sketchfab URL is **not** enough. Confirm `isDownloadable` and a redistributable `license.slug` on:

```
GET https://api.sketchfab.com/v3/models/{uid}
```

## Download

```
GET https://api.sketchfab.com/v3/models/{uid}/download
```

Write the short-lived `glb.url` to `public/models/{id}/model.glb` immediately. Do not cache that URL.

## License (must ship)

OK: **CC0** (`cc0`), **CC-BY** (`by`), **CC-BY-SA** (`by-sa`).  
Not OK: Editorial (`ed`), Standard (`st`), NC (`by-nc`, `by-nc-sa`), store-only, `isDownloadable: false`.

If the requested model is Editorial/Standard, search for a downloadable CC stand-in and note the substitution in that model’s `license.json` `notes`.

## Creator preference

1. Search with `&user=nazidefenseforceofficial` first.
2. Use that creator when a suitable downloadable CC model exists.
3. Otherwise pick the best downloadable CC match (recognizable silhouette, prefer ≲200k tris, no huge terrain/ground plane).

## Wire-up

1. Download the GLB via the API into `public/models/{id}/model.glb` and write `license.json`.
2. Run `npm run compress-models -- --only={id}` (no-ops if already Draco/meshopt).
3. Add the item to `src/data/catalog.ts` (meters + `yawDegrees` so +Z is nose) and tags in `src/data/catalogTags.ts`.
4. Inspect in the viewer at Facing 0°: silhouette cropped, sitting on the ground, scale vs person-male (1.75 m).
5. Run `npm run sync-attributions`.
6. **Commit** the compressed `model.glb` and `license.json`.
